      "message": "This relies on the IDnsResolver.TRANSPORT_* constants always being the same as the NetworkCapabilities.TRANSPORT_* constants. We should do one of the following:\n\n1. Have an explicit conversion function that converts between NetworkCapabilities.TRANSPORT_xxx to IDnsResolver.TRANSPORT_xxx, and call it for each element of the array.\n2. Write a test that ensures that NetworkCapabilities.TRANSPORT_xxx \u003d\u003d IDnsResolver.TRANSPORT_xxx for every possible value of each.\n\nFor #2, I don\u0027t think you can write those tests in C++, but you can have a Java test that depends on netd_aidl_interface-unstable-java (or -v3, once this is frozen) and simply does:\n\n    assertEquals(NetworkCapabilites.TRANSPORT_CELLULAR, IDnsResolver.TRANSPORT_CELLULAR);\n    assertEquals(NetworkCapabilites.TRANSPORT_WIFI, IDnsResolver.TRANSPORT_WIFI);\n    ...\n\nor something equivalent but more elegant like reflection into the generated class.",
